---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { docsUrl } from "../../site";
---

<Base
  title="Installation"
  description="How to install LibreDental on Windows or Linux, where your data is stored, and how to load demo data."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Installation and first run</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Install the desktop app on Windows or Linux. For several workstations
      sharing one database, see the office server setup at the bottom.
    </p>

    <h2>Requirements</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Windows 10 or 11, or a 64-bit Linux distribution (x64 or ARM64).</li>
      <li>macOS is not supported at the moment.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Install</h2>
    <p>Get the file for your system from the <a href="/download/">download page</a>.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Windows:</strong> run the installer. It uses the WebView2
        runtime, which Windows 10 and 11 already include.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Debian / Ubuntu:</strong> <code>sudo apt install ./libredental-linux-amd64.deb</code></li>
      <li><strong>Fedora / openSUSE:</strong> <code>sudo dnf install ./libredental-linux-amd64.rpm</code></li>
      <li><strong>Arch:</strong> <code>sudo pacman -U libredental-linux-amd64.pkg.tar.zst</code></li>
      <li>
        <strong>Any distribution:</strong> make the AppImage executable with
        <code>chmod +x libredental-linux-amd64.AppImage</code>, then run it.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="muted">On ARM64, use the matching <code>arm64</code> file names.</p>

    <h2>Where your data lives</h2>
    <p>
      LibreDental stores everything in a <code>LibreDental</code> folder in your
      user configuration directory:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Linux: <code>~/.config/LibreDental</code></li>
      <li>Windows: <code>%AppData%\LibreDental</code></li>
    </ul>
    <p>To back up, copy that folder somewhere safe while the app is closed.</p>

    <h2 id="demo-data">Try it with demo data</h2>
    <p>
      The demo archives on the <a href="/download/">download page</a> contain a
      fictional practice. To load one:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>Close LibreDental.</li>
      <li>Back up your existing <code>LibreDental</code> folder (see above).</li>
      <li>Extract the archive's <code>LibreDental</code> folder in its place.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Office server (several workstations)</h2>
    <p>
      The server runs on one central PC, and other workstations use it from a
      web browser. Setup covers firewall rules, a static IP and keeping the PC
      awake, all in the <a href={`${docsUrl}/lan-server-setup.md`}
        >LAN server setup guide</a
      >.
    </p>

    <hr />
    <p><a href="/docs/">← Back to documentation</a></p>
  </div>
</Base>
